     "rate": "+0%",
     "text": "In nineteen hundred and nine, Paris almost tore down the Eiffel Tower. Workers built the framework as a temporary centerpiece for the eighteen eighty-nine World's Fair on a strict twenty-year permit. Workers assembled the massive iron lattice using two point five million rivets across two years, two months, and five days. City officials intended to scrap the entire monument once the permit expired, returning the Champ de Mars to empty ground. Engineers mounted radio and wireless telegraph antennas at its top, turning the doomed tower into a high-altitude transmitter. Military commanders tested those wireless signals across the city, proving the structure indispensable for national defense. Wrecking crews stayed away permanently because the antenna kept the iron giant standing."
